`AV_ERROR_MAX_STRING_SIZE` is only 64 so I think it's ok:

```c++
  text.resize(AV_ERROR_MAX_STRING_SIZE);
  av_strerror(err, text.data(), text.size());
```

If it were a much larger number (1000, 2000) then it would be better to do what neo1973 says to avoid always returning a string of maximum length.:

```c++
  char buffer[AV_ERROR_MAX_STRING_SIZE];
  av_strerror(err, buffer, sizeof(buffer));
  std::string text(buffer);
  return text;
```

